VMC %s is in %d fragments. Continue with Memory Card in slot %d?
Back up the VMC to a PC, remove it from the device, then copy it back. If it is still fragmented, free space and retry. Never delete your only copy.
Entrambi
Questo server UDPBD/UDPFS è di sola lettura, quindi non è possibile usarvi una VMC. Il gioco salva sulla vera memory card.
In-Game Menu (Beta)
The IGR combo pauses the game under a menu: Resume, Cheats, Exit Game, Power Off. OPL core games on a real PS2 only; where it cannot draw, the combo leaves the game as before.
IGR Combo
The buttons that leave a game (OPL core games). Press to record your own: hold at least 3 buttons for 3 seconds. With your own combo, the usual combos are left to the game, and only the IGR Power-Off Combo (if set) or the power button powers off.
IGR Power-Off Combo
Off by default. Press to record buttons that power the console off from a game (OPL core games): hold at least 3 buttons for 3 seconds. It must differ from the IGR Combo.
Hold the buttons for your power-off combo (at least 3) for 3 seconds. Hold Triangle alone for 5 seconds to turn it off. Hold Circle alone for 5 seconds to cancel.
The IGR Combo and the IGR Power-Off Combo must use different buttons. Nothing was changed.
Hold the buttons for your IGR combo (at least 3) for 3 seconds. Hold Triangle alone for 5 seconds to go back to the usual combo (L1+L2+R1+R2+Start+Select). Hold Circle alone for 5 seconds to cancel.
Back to the usual combo
Turn off
Grid Layout
Covers per page in the Grid view: the theme's own, or a preset. A 16:9 picture fits more columns, and each preset shows the shape it has on the picture now. Grid (7x2) keeps its own shape.
Compact
Library
Pages
Pages gives every device its own tab. All Games List puts the games of every started device, PS2, PS1 and apps, on one page. Same setting as All Games List under Game Sources.
Copy out as PSU
Copies the picked save into the folder as one .psu file, the save file uLaunchELF, EMS and Apollo use. The card is not changed.
This .psu file is cut short or is not a PS2 save.
